Track 2: "Who Forgave the Courier at Bir-Haddad?"
- Story & Context: Huddled beneath an acoustic-foam canopy at the Bir-Haddad trade post, the aging courier Selim washed the bitter taste of salted goat butter tea from his tongue and confessed his forty-year secret to the caravan elders. He revealed that he had deliberately delayed an urgent marriage missive, slipping the thick folded vellum inside an Access Virus B synthesizer chassis to shim a vibrating resonance pot so the off-beat dancehall skanks wouldn't slip out of tune. Amina played a muted, velvet French horn solo that sounded like an apology dragged through magnetic tape dust while the sub-bass thudded like a remorseful heart, prompting Selim to sing the cracking refrain: "I kept your yes inside the filter bank." The caravan refused to exile him, choosing instead to loop his taped confession until dawn softened the desert.
